    "description": "# DL-6: Link Validation Logic\n\n_Confirm how Assignment Cap enforcement is split between Salesforce and the CMS, so no redundant validation gets built._\n\n### AUTOMATION\n\n* Assignment Cap enforcement happens on the CMS side, not Salesforce\n\n* Salesforce's only job is to pass Assignment Cap and Active to the CMS; the CMS blocks over-cap assignments at the point of actual link assignment\n\n### IMPLEMENTATION REQUIREMENTS\n\n* No Salesforce-side validation logic needs to be built for this story. Salesforce passes Assignment Cap and Active to the CMS; the CMS enforces the cap at the point of link assignment.\n\n### NOTES\n\n* Provenance: DL-6 (Deal Record User Stories doc).\n* Scope here is confirming/documenting the SF → CMS field hand-off, not building enforcement logic in Salesforce.\n\n### SOURCE\n\n* [Deal Record User Stories — Google Doc](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IIfaPIol2HmX8v09gw0SKQyCuoHTiwrJxdDNc7qtvB8/edit)\n* [Aug 18 Weekly Sync — Joyce Kiddell, 42:15 (confirms CMS-side enforcement, no SF validation)](https://fathom.video/calls/787411922?timestamp=2535)\n* Dependencies: [BUILD-216 — Deal: Link Object + Assignment Fields (toggle)](https://app.asana.com/0/0/1217693812480978/f/)\n* Owner (proposed): Taryn Reithofer\n* Created 2026-08-20 from Deal record documentation review.\n\n",
